{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - Lifecycle - User - Okta User Deactivated, Suspended or Deleted",
	"Description": "An Okta user was deactivated, suspended, or deleted. Offboarding looks like this, and so does an adversary locking out the account of someone who would have noticed them, or removing the account they used once they have a better one.\n\nEvent types: user.lifecycle.deactivate, user.lifecycle.suspend, user.lifecycle.delete.initiated, user.lifecycle.delete.completed\n\nReference(s):\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/api/openapi/okta-management/management/tag/SystemLog/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
